Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient with mocked fetch and mock-mode verification

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with comprehensive vitest tests that mock global fetch (no real network calls). Cover: URL/header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error handling, missing/empty API key errors, malformed response validation, private apiKey field, constructor precedence, mock-mode activation and strictness, and ensure real failures are never silently masked by mock data.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts contains ≥5 vitest tests using mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) with afterEach fetch restoration, covering: (a) correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, (b) successful response parsed into FlightResult[], (c) HTTP 4xx rejection with status code in error message, (d) missing API key constructor error, (e) malformed response body parse/validation error
- Test verifies apiKey is stored as a private field and is not publicly readable on the SkyscannerClient instance
- Test verifies empty-string apiKey and empty-string RAPIDAPI_KEY both throw the same missing-key Error as when apiKey is omitted entirely
- Test verifies constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var when both are present
- Test verifies Error on HTTP 4xx/5xx does not include the apiKey value in its message string
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true': searchFlights returns deterministic fixture and global fetch spy/assertion confirms fetch was never invoked
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API with non-'true' values ('false', '1', 'TRUE', empty string, unset) performs the real fetch call — mock mode is strict opt-in, not a fuzzy truthy check
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 with no type errors; vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class name is SkyscannerClient, exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor(opts: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws exact error: 'SkyscannerClient: missing API key. Provide `apiKey` to the constructor or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when both opts.apiKey and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var are missing/empty
- API key resolution order: opts.apiKey (trimmed) takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var (trimmed)
- Empty string apiKey (after trim) and empty string RAPIDAPI_KEY both trigger the same missing key error
- Private field #apiKey stores the resolved key; no public getter exists
- Method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- adults defaults to 1 when omitted in URL construction: adults=${encodeURIComponent(String(params.adults ?? 1))}
- Mock mode activated only when process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string equality, not truthy)
- Mock mode returns deterministic fixture from buildMockResults() with 3 flights, no fetch call made
- Non-'true' MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API values (false, 1, TRUE, empty, unset) result in real fetch call
- RapidAPI URL: https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/flights/search-roundtrip
- Query params: from, to, date, adults (not origin/destination)
- Request headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key', 'X-RapidAPI-Host', 'Accept': 'application/json'
- HTTP error message format: 'Skyscanner API request failed with HTTP ${status} ${statusText}' - apiKey is intentionally NOT included
- JSON parse error message format: 'Failed to parse Skyscanner API response body as JSON: ${reason}'
- Validation error prefix: 'Failed to parse flight result at index ${index}: ' or 'Failed to parse flight result at index ${index}: 'expected an object, got ...'
- Response body validation: expects array or object containing array via #extractFlightArray
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- ensureFlightResult validates: price is finite number, currency is non-empty string, airline is non-empty string, departure is non-empty string, arrival is non-empty string, duration is finite number, stops is non-negative integer

